## Decision
When sync is enabled, `serve` checks whether the iCloud-hosted rules file is a symlink and refuses to proceed if it is. This is a guard against following a link to an unintended location. A symlink could point outside the iCloud container, so reading or writing through it could touch files the user did not intend, or break sync assumptions. Failing early with a refusal is safer than resolving the link silently. The details of the implementation (error wording, exact check) are not available from the slice.

